[M2] (golly 2.6)
#C 3-digit hexadecimal counter.
#C
#C Starting from the right, a p4600 signal passes through 2 period 
#C doublers, raising the period to p18400. Each digit contains 4
#C consecutive period-doublers, each which sends a signal to a memory
#C unit (the things above the Herchel track). Each memory unit stores
#C 1 bit of the digit, and an LWSS travelling upwards alternates its
#C state. Each memory unit contains a HWSS gun, which feeds a toggle
#C switch (the 4 large things which send MWSSes into the conversion
#C table. This conversion table converts the binary value into a
#C hexadecimal value). It is reflected into an MWSS stream, where
#C it travels on the left side of the digit. It then enters another
#C conversion table, which transforms the hexadecimal value into
#C 7-segment code. The streams of LWSSes travel right into the display
#C digit. Each segment contains 2 anti-parallel lines of "glider out
#C of the blue" reactions. These fill the segment with an array of
#C gliders.
#C
#C Runs best in Golly, using hashlife at a speed of 8^5.
#C Can be viewed completely at 1/8 zoom, but the digits appear solid
#C at 1/32 zoom.
#C
#C Herschel track generated in Hersrch, and p46 circuitry obtained 
#C mainly from the patterns "p46racetrack" and "OTCAmetapixel".
#C
#C Made by Calcyman (2008)
#R B3/S23
